    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this May 8th slate, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Josh Naylor** (67.01) anchor our offense, both enjoying favorable matchups against Burke, S. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is our strongest start, benefiting from a 4.45 xERA on the opposing mound and a massive +14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage, while **Josh Naylor** leverages a clean path in the cleanup spot to provide stability. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** and **James Wood** offer high-ceiling upside; **Tyler Soderstrom** is primed for a breakout with a +16% park factor adjustment in his favor, and **James Wood** continues to command his spot at the top of the order, maintaining a 61.94 score despite a neutral platoon stance against the lefty.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Kyle Karros**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 39.67 score, falling just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. While his platoon edge against Luzardo was enticing, the combination of a tough 3.20 xERA and a stifling defensive battery behind the dish suppressed his efficiency. We remain cautious with **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** today; **Brice Turang** faces an elite hold pitcher in Fried that limits his stolen base ceiling, and **Corbin Carroll** is battling a sub-3.00 xERA matchup against McLean. We are keeping a close watch on the defensive metrics\u2014specifically the 1.87s pop time catchers facing **Corbin Carroll**\u2014as we hunt for those high-leverage stolen bases that define our 5x5 strategy. **Giancarlo Stanton** remains sidelined, and we will continue to preserve our limited game caps by keeping **Jose Caballero** and **Travis Bazzana** benched until their projected efficiency clears our threshold.",
